1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:07,900
0 V can mean dead. Or a broken tester.

2
00:00:08,200 --> 00:00:15,900
Step 1: test the tester on a known source. It shows voltage.

3
00:00:16,200 --> 00:00:24,900
Step 2: measure at the work point, between all conductors and to earth.

4
00:00:25,200 --> 00:00:33,900
Step 3: test again on the known source. The tester still works.

5
00:00:34,200 --> 00:00:40,900
Only then do you know that 0 V means dead.
